hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20604","Waki' narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar al-Abdi, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a sickly man, so permit me a jarrah vessel in which to make nabidh. He said: So he permitted him in it."
"20605","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar al-Abdi, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will not come until tribes are swallowed by the earth, until it is said: Who remains of Banu so-and-so. So I knew he meant the Arabs, for the non-Arabs are only attributed to their villages."
